&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Product Manager (Hardware Security &amp;amp; IP)&lt;br&gt;Reports to: VP of Product Management&lt;br&gt;Department: Product Management&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;Location: Netherlands, France, Germany, Spain, Austria, Netherlands, UK, Belgium&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;💼 About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;PQShield is looking for an Experienced IP Product Manager to expand our Product team.&amp;nbsp;Candidates should hold a degree in Electronic Engineering/Computer Science or equivalent. We&amp;nbsp;hope that you have at least 7 years of experience, but also an open, research-oriented mindset.&amp;nbsp;*This is a highly technical role, and you will sit at the critical intersection of software,&amp;nbsp;firmware, and hardware architecture, hence you must have experience with embedded&amp;nbsp;software, security architecture, and/or digital design. We would welcome applications from&amp;nbsp;Engineers, Security Architects, Design Engineers who are looking to move into Product&amp;nbsp;Management.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;We have been established since 2018, so you would be directly working with the founders and&amp;nbsp;inventors of this deep tech startup. Technology is already a couple of years in the making, its&amp;nbsp;feasibility having been established, funding secured, and it has a clear path to market. This is a&amp;nbsp;great opportunity &amp;nbsp;for career progression and to get a head start in a rapidly expanding segment of the semiconductor industry (Post-Quantum Cryptography and RISC-V).&amp;nbsp;Our platform IP components come together as a RISC-V MCU based Sub-system with advanced&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;post-quantum) cryptography algorithm support and security features.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;⚒️ What you’ll be doing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with key customers and ecosystem partners to integrate our security solutions into&amp;nbsp;broader system architectures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the primary bridge between hardware engineering, software/firmware teams,&amp;nbsp;security architects, and business stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to critically prioritize product backlogs, balance technical debt with commercial&amp;nbsp;features, and make tough trade-offs between area, power, performance, and security&amp;nbsp;(PPAS).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Author comprehensive Product Requirement Documents (PRDs) and technical&amp;nbsp;specifications that translate complex cryptographic standards into actionable hardware&amp;nbsp;engineering requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and drive the multi-year product roadmap for hardware security IPs and&amp;nbsp;cryptographic solutions, aligning with market trends and customer requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct market research and competitive analysis to identify customer needs, market&amp;nbsp;opportunities, and industry trends related to Post-Quantum Cryptography for platform&amp;nbsp;security and hardware accelerators&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define product requirements, features, and roadmaps for our entire product portfolio of&amp;nbsp;hardware products based on customer feedback, market insights, and latest technology&amp;nbsp;developments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with tech leads and sales to align product roadmaps&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Measure product performance utilising data from internal and other data sources&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuous improvement of our product development processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🎯 Required Skills And Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven hands-on experience with integration of hardware security IP and architectures&amp;nbsp;such as Arm, RISC-V, or x86, TRNG, PUF, masking, blinding, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;System architect mind set able to envision products with end-to-end security integration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of the semiconductor industry products, security IP market&amp;nbsp;dynamics, and related technologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid understanding of modern silicon manufacturing processes, physical design&amp;nbsp;constraints, and post-silicon bring-up/validation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep familiarity with SoC (System-on-Chip) architecture, bus protocols (AXI, AHB),&amp;nbsp;and hardware-software interfaces.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A background that includes transitioning from a Hardware Design/Verification Enginee&amp;nbsp;or Security Architect into Product Management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🌟 Preferred Skills and Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of successfully launching and managing complex security IP products&amp;nbsp;throughout their lifecycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with hardware security industry standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with hardware security certifications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of Industry standard SoC Security Architectures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of tamper resistance and/or power side-channel security countermeasures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working on secure element or smart cards designs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using Gitlab CI, or otherwise principles of continuous integration and testing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🏆Some of the perks of working with us:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Unparalleled opportunities to learn and accelerated career development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A collaborative, team environment with people who truly love what they do.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Co

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Isomorphic Labs is applying frontier AI to help unlock deeper scientific insights, faster breakthroughs, and life-changing medicines with an ambition to solve all disease.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The future is coming. A future enabled and enriched by the incredible power of machine learning. A future in which diseases are curtailed or cured starting with better and faster drug discovery.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Come and be part of an interdisciplinary team driving groundbreaking innovation and play a meaningful role in contributing towards us achieving our ambitious goals, while being a part of an inspiring and collaborative culture.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The world we want tomorrow is the one we’re building today. It starts with the culture at this company. It starts with you.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Iso&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Isomorphic Labs (IsoLabs) was launched in 2021 to advance human health by building on and beyond the Nobel-winning AlphaFold system. Since then, our interdisciplinary team of drug discovery experts and machine learning specialists has built powerful new predictive and generative AI models that accelerate scientific discovery at digital speed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our name comes from the belief that there is an underlying symmetry between biology and information science. By harnessing AI’s powerful capabilities, we can use it to model complex biological phenomena to help design novel molecules, anticipate how drugs will perform and develop innovative medicines to treat and cure some of the world’s most devastating diseases.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We have built a world-leading drug design engine comprising AI models that are capable of working across multiple therapeutic areas and drug modalities. We are continually innovating on model architecture and developing cutting-edge capabilities to advance rational drug design.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Every day, and with each new breakthrough, we’re getting closer to the promise of digital biology, and achieving our ambitious mission to one day solve all disease with the help of AI.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Impact&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are building the largest foundation models in biotech and applying them immediately to cure disease. You will play a pivotal role in ensuring the reliability and scalability of the foundations that make this possible.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Principal Engineer, you will lead the efforts to harden our systems, ensuring our groundbreaking AI is built on an unshakeable base, working closely with the research team and the Applied ML teams to ensure the infrastructure is stable, reliable and can operate with more data and larger models as we grow.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and operate our inference platform, serving fleets of cutting-edge machine learning models to scientific applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design strategy and build roadmaps for maturing the platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Architect and optimize our next-generation inference services. You will solve core scaling limits, ensuring high-throughput performance and feature parity across our model serving stack.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to core technical decisions on tooling and architectural design while partnering with science, product, and operations teams to align infrastructure with biotech R&amp;amp;D cycles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver high-quality and well-tested user-focused features.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills and Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience in architecting and managing large-scale AI/ML workloads in a production environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expertise in cloud compute design, specifically within Google Cloud Platform (GCP).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Orchestration: Significant experience deploying and managing complex workloads within Kubernetes (GKE).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional familiarity with NVIDIA GPU generations and the intricacies of high-performance compute.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong programming skills and a &quot;reliability-first&quot; approach to software development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to Have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A career history that spans both ML Software Engineering and Infrastructure SRE roles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading multi-disciplinary projects and navigating complex stakeholder requirements in a fast-paced environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with workload scheduling, ML efficiency research, and hardware benchmarking.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Google TPU generations and specialized ML-driven R&amp;amp;D cycles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Culture and values&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are guided by our shared values. It&#39;s not about finding people who think and act in the same way. These values help to guide our work and will continue to strengthen it.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Thoughtful&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Thoughtful at Iso is about curiosity, creativity and care. It is about good people doing good, rigorous and future-making science every single day.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Brave&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Brave at Iso is about fearlessness, but it’s also about initiative and integrity. The scale of the challenge demands nothing less.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Determined&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot

&lt;h5&gt;We are looking for a Director of Engineering to join the AI Practice Efficiency team.&lt;/h5&gt;
&lt;h5&gt;Your mission will be to define and deliver how AI transforms the daily work of healthcare professionals — across intelligent scheduling, automated document processing, smart task management, and AI-assisted patient communication. You will lead teams building AI-powered features across two horizons: augmenting existing practice workflows with intelligent capabilities, and pioneering net-new AI-native products that unlock entirely new value for practitioners and their patients. Working in the tech team at Doctolib means building innovative products and features that improve the daily lives of care teams and patients across Europe.&lt;/h5&gt;
&lt;h5&gt;What you&#39;ll do:&lt;/h5&gt;
&lt;h5&gt;Your responsibilities include but are not limited to:&lt;/h5&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;h5&gt;Lead and scale 1 engineering team owning the AI Practice Efficiency scope: manage teams delivering AI features across practice workflows — intelligent scheduling, automated document processing, smart task management, and AI-assisted patient communication. Champion delivers excellence by unblocking teams, setting high execution standards, and accelerating the pace of experimentation and production release, with an initial focus on the Phone assistant, currently one of Doctolib&#39;s most strategic product bets that we need to grow.&lt;/h5&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;h5&gt;Define and execute the AI product-engineering strategy: in close partnership with Product, Data Science, and Design, set the technical direction for AI Practice Efficiency — deciding when to build vs. buy, how to evaluate and select foundation models, when to fine-tune, and how to architect for safety, explainability, and regulatory compliance. Balance ambitious AI innovation with pragmatic, high-quality execution.&lt;/h5&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;h5&gt;Own responsible AI delivery in a regulated context: ensure AI features are built with appropriate safeguards for a healthcare environment, covering evaluation frameworks, human-in-the-loop design, data privacy (GDPR/HDS), explainability, and bias mitigation. Serve as the engineering voice ensuring our AI products meet the trust bar that healthcare professionals and patients require. Work together with the VP of Engineering of the Domain to set the AI strategy for the domain.&lt;/h5&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;h5&gt;Drive cross-domain AI adoption and platform thinking: collaborate with other engineering streams and the broader AI platform teams to ensure shared AI infrastructure, tooling, and evaluation frameworks both benefit from — and contribute to — your teams&#39; work. Champion AI-augmented engineering practices within your own teams as a forcing function for productivity and quality.&lt;/h5&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h5&gt;Who you are&lt;/h5&gt;
&lt;h5&gt;Before you read on: if you don&#39;t have the exact profile described below, but you feel this job description matches your skill set, we still encourage you to apply.&lt;/h5&gt;
&lt;h5&gt;You&#39;ll be a great fit if you:&lt;/h5&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;h5&gt;Have at least 12+ years of engineering experience, with significant time leading managers and senior ICs in fast-paced, high-growth technology environments — and a proven ability to run multiple teams across complex, interdependent scopes without losing clarity on outcomes&lt;/h5&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;h5&gt;Have a track record of shipping AI or ML-powered features to real users at scale, with full lifecycle ownership: from problem framing and data requirements through model evaluation, integration, monitoring, and iteration&lt;/h5&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;h5&gt;Stay close to the craft: you use AI tools directly, can build working prototypes to pressure-test ideas, and are hands-on with LLM integration, RAG architectures, fine-tuning tradeoffs, evaluation frameworks, and inference constraints — you see prototyping as a leadership tool&lt;/h5&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;h5&gt;Bring sharp product instinct for where AI creates genuine clinical value, combined with a clear framework for navigating responsible AI delivery in a regulated, high-trust healthcare context (GDPR/HDS, explainability, human oversight)&lt;/h5&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;h5&gt;Are an exceptional people leader: you deliberately adapt your leadership approach based on context, actively mentor other managers, and build environments where engineers grow and AI craftsmanship continuously rises&lt;/h5&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;h5&gt;Are fluent in English&lt;/h5&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h5&gt;It would be fantastic if you:&lt;/h5&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;h5&gt;Have experience building AI in healthcare, financial services, or another domain where safety, explainability, and auditability are non-negotiable&lt;/h5&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;h5&gt;Have shipped AI that touches clinical workflows, medical terminology, or patient-facing communications&lt;/h5&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;h5&gt;Have experience building AI products that work across languages and regulatory frameworks&lt;/h5&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
